```python
def mobius(d):
    result, q = 1, 2
    while q * q <= d:
        if d % q == 0:
            d //= q
            if d % q == 0:
                return 0
            result = -result
        q += 1
    return -result if d > 1 else result

def count_irreducible(p, n):
    total = sum(mobius(d) * p ** (n // d) for d in range(1, n + 1) if n % d == 0)
    return total // n
```

The formula comes from $X^{p^n} - X = \prod_{d \mid n} \prod_{f \text{ irreducible, } \deg f = d} f$, whose degrees give $p^n = \sum_{d \mid n} d\,N(d)$; Möbius inversion turns this into Gauss's formula. Since $N(n) \ge \frac1n(p^n - \sum_{d \lt n} p^d) \gt 0$, irreducible polynomials of every degree exist — which gives another proof that $\mathbb{F}_{p^n}$ exists.
